  "title": "How does a tsunami form? 🌊",
  "hook": "How does a tsunami form, a wave that can cross entire oceans?",
  "presenter": "perro",
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "role": "hook",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_hook",
      "narration": "How does a tsunami form, a wave that can cross entire oceans?",
      "on_screen_text": "How is a tsunami born?",
      "highlight_words": [
        "tsunami"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_quake",
      "narration": "Most start with a big earthquake under the sea, when a plate suddenly lurches upward.",
      "on_screen_text": "An undersea earthquake",
      "highlight_words": [
        "earthquake"
      ],
      "sfx": "impact",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_lift",
      "narration": "That pushes up the entire column of water, from the seafloor to the surface.",
      "on_screen_text": "All the water rises",
      "highlight_words": [
        "All"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_spread",
      "narration": "The water drops back down and the energy spreads out as waves in every direction.",
      "on_screen_text": "Waves in every direction",
      "highlight_words": [
        "every"
      ],
      "sfx": "whoosh",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_speed",
      "narration": "In deep water they travel at about eight hundred kilometers per hour, as fast as a jet.",
      "on_screen_text": "As fast as a jet",
      "highlight_words": [
        "jet"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_small",
      "narration": "But out at sea they're barely noticeable: a meter tall or less, and a ship hardly feels them.",
      "on_screen_text": "Nearly invisible at sea",
      "highlight_words": [
        "invisible"
      ],
      "sfx": "none",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_grow",
      "narration": "Near the coast, the water gets shallow: the wave slows down and grows into a giant.",
      "on_screen_text": "It slows and grows",
      "highlight_words": [
        "grows"
      ],
      "sfx": "riser",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "role": "development",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_retreat",
      "narration": "A warning sign: if the sea suddenly pulls back, don't go look; get to high ground.",
      "on_screen_text": "If the sea pulls back, go up!",
      "highlight_words": [
        "up!"
      ],
      "sfx": "ding",
      "transition": "cut"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "role": "surprise",
      "type": "scene3d",
      "model3d": "tsu_pacific",
      "narration": "In nineteen sixty, a tsunami born in Chile crossed the whole Pacific and reached Japan about twenty-two hours later.",
      "on_screen_text": "From Chile to Japan",
      "highlight_words": [
        "Japan"
