  "description": "Most tsunamis come from large undersea earthquakes that lift the seafloor and the whole water column. In deep water they travel at about 800 km/h and are a meter tall or less, but near the coast they slow down and grow. If the sea suddenly pulls back, get to high ground. In 1960 a tsunami from Chile reached Japan about 22 hours later. Original 3D animation; general information, always follow local authorities.",
